{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246528-question-pledges-and-freehold-justice","id":246528,"title":"Question: pledges and freehold justice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-01T18:38:03-07:00","id":246528,"title":"Question: pledges and freehold justice","content":"I have 2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Can the forbiddance task of a pledge be to not lie? The definition of lying could be fuzzy (exaggeration is technically lying), and I don't think the wyrd can judge intention (forbiddance from saying anything with the attempt to deceive wouldn't fly), but what about forbiddance from a simple yes/no kind of lie? I ask because if that is allowed (and it seems to me it should be based on the other examples given) it has implications for a freehold justice system. Namely, if a changeling is suspected of some crime, the King or Queen could demand that changeling swear such a pledge before questioning and their guilt or innocence will be almost assuredly revealed. Refusal to swear the oath would be as bad as admitting to guilt. Now a ruler could certainly abuse the power to demand a changeling swear this pledge by asking about personal or political stuff, but if the questioned changeling doesn't have to answer any particular question if he/she (and/or witnesses) feels it is unfair. So it seems obvious to me that any freehold would use such a pledge in their justice system, and therefore it would be very difficult for a changeling to get away with any significant crime against the freehold. I could see a paranoid ruler demanding such pledges randomly with a &quot;if you have nothing to hide, you have nothing to fear&quot; sort of philosophy. So yea, this makes it hard to have blatantly antagonistic changelings (privateers, loyalists, bridge-burners, etc.) within the freehold because they surely can't get away with much crime before being discovered. As a side note, one could ask the same question for justice in VtR, where a kindred with Auspex could detect lies. But in that case it's a contested action so the lier may get away with it, and the lie is only apparent to the kindred with Auspex whereas the pledge sanction could be chosen such that the breaking of the pledge is obvious to all witnesses. <br /> <br /> 2) I don't understand what determines the willpower cost to seal a pledge. Looking at the examples, the willpower cost is 1 per changeling that is swearing the pledge, plus any extras in the description of the tasks, boons, sanctions, or durance of the pledge. But then the Oath of the Rose and Thorn demands a willpower point from the mortal, which is not described as an added cost for the ensorcellment task (the glamor cost is). So yea, does the book clearly defines this somewhere?<br /> <br /> Thank you for any input! If this has been discussed elsewhere, please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3753-miffinmix","name":"MiffinMix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T11:12:27-07:00","id":246964,"title":"","content":"A forbiddence from lying, or using the &quot;true tongue&quot; flaw as a sanction should be well within the abilities of pledges. That being said, fairy tales which emphasize that the fey can't tell a direct lie do so usually by highlighting how amazingly deceptive they are anyway. And that's ignoring the political ramifications of invading privacy and a court politician demanding no one else lie. It may effectively screen at the door for loyalists and privateers, but then the enemies will just get more clever and internal dissent will strain the freehold. I'd least I'd think that the most likely outcome - and it does make a good story. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}